From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] linux_boot: put the console on the framebuffer too

Adds console=tty0 before ttyGS3 so printk mirrors to the AMOLED as well as the
USB port, which is what makes the panel show the boot log and the login prompt
instead of the driver's last painted image.

Order still matters: /dev/console binds to the LAST console= on the line, so
ttyGS3 stays last and init's stdin/stdout remain on the USB port. tty0 is a sink
only -- there is no keyboard behind it, and the side buttons emit keycodes that
nothing consumes yet.

Apply from the esp-hosted checkout root (its git repo root is build/esp-hosted,
not the esp_driver subdirectory):

    cd build/esp-hosted
    git apply -p1 ../../patches/app/0001-linux-boot-console-tty0.patch

It has to be committed there too: esp_driver/CMakeLists.txt runs
`git reset --hard` on every cmake invocation, so an uncommitted change is lost
at the next build.

diff --git a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/linux_boot.c b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/linux_boot.c
index 4cc4e02..30efbe3 100644
--- a/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/linux_boot.c
+++ b/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/linux_boot.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ static const char default_cmdline[] =
 	 * line. With ttyS0 last, init's stdin/stdout went to a UART this board
 	 * does not have, while printk still mirrored to ttyGS3 -- so the log
 	 * appeared and typing went nowhere. */
-	"console=ttyS0,115200n8 console=ttyGS3 "
+	"console=ttyS0,115200n8 console=tty0 console=ttyGS3 "
 	"rw root=mtd:rootfs rootfstype=cramfs panic=10 panic_console_replay "
 	"loglevel=7";
 
